        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And behold, now it came to pass that when the Lord had spoken these words unto Nephi, he did stop and did not go unto his own house, but did return unto the multitudes who were scattered about upon the face of the land, and began to declare unto them the word of the Lord which had been spoken unto him, concerning their destruction if they did not repent.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 10:12",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Now behold, notwithstanding that great miracle which Nephi had done in telling them concerning the death of the chief judge, they did harden their hearts and did not hearken unto the words of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "Mark 6:6 (4–6)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 10:13",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore Nephi did declare unto them the word of the Lord, saying: Except ye repent, thus saith the Lord, ye shall be smitten even unto destruction.",
        "footNotes": [
